Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?dos:=20Phase=2010=20patch=200047=20=E2=80=94=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?DSP-mediated=20WaveBlaster=20MIDI=20(default)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

W22-WB-F MPUPROBE forensic analysis (docs/MPUPROBE-W22WB-F-ANALYSIS.md)
established three essential findings about the g2k Vibra16S+S2 WB
hardware that invalidate the patch-0044 direct-port default:

1. **MPU-401 status register bit 7 (TX-READY) lies on this chip.** In
   probe section 9, polling bit 7 for 5000 iterations never saw it
   clear; immediately afterward in section 10, an outportb to the same
   port succeeded without any wait. Any code that gates writes on
   TX-READY-clear hangs indefinitely. Patch 0044's blind-init avoided
   this by not polling, but section-9-style direct-port writes are
   still vulnerable when SDL is concurrently running.

2. **MPU-401 IRQ never fires in UART mode** on this chip -- mixer reg
   0x82 stayed at 0x30 across 12 byte dispatches. UART output is
   strictly poll-only; specifically poll the DSP write-status (port
   0x22D bit 7) which IS reliable, NOT the MPU status which lies.

3. **Both direct-port (Option A) and DSP-mediated (Option B) MIDI
   dispatch paths work in isolation** (probe sections 9 + 10 dispatched
   note_on/note_off + 500ms hold without lockup). The W22-WB-C/D/F
   hangs are SDL-orchestration issues, most plausibly cross-firmware
   concurrency between direct-port MPU access and DSP DMA programming
   during SDL audio init.

Pivot to DSP-mediated MIDI (Option B from the analysis) as the new
default. DSP-mediated funnels ALL chip access through one bus
contender (the DSP write port at base+0xC), eliminating the
cross-firmware race entirely. The chip sees a single coherent stream
of DSP commands; there's no second bus contender to deadlock against.

Sequence per Creative SB16 reference + probe-validated:
  - Enter UART mode: SDL_DOSAudioSB_DSPMidiEnterUART (DSP cmd 0x34)
  - Per MIDI byte: SDL_DOSAudioSB_DSPMidiWriteByte (DSP cmd 0x38 + byte)
  - No teardown DSP command needed (SoundManager::shutdown's
    DOSSOUNDBLASTER_CloseDevice issues 0xD3 to silence the speaker
    which silences MIDI output alongside DAC).

New SB16-backend exports (vendor/SDL/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c):
  - SDL_DOSAudioSB_IsInitialized() -- checks soundblaster_base_port
    >= 0 (i.e., DOSSOUNDBLASTER_OpenDevice ran successfully).
  - SDL_DOSAudioSB_DSPMidiEnterUART() -- calls the existing static
    WriteSoundBlasterDSP(0x34). The DSP write-status (port 0x22D bit
    7) timeout in WriteSoundBlasterDSP is 100000 iterations and
    reliable per W22-WB-F probe section 10 evidence.
  - SDL_DOSAudioSB_DSPMidiWriteByte(byte) -- issues 0x38 + byte via
    two WriteSoundBlasterDSP calls.

Declarations live in vendor/SDL/src/core/dos/SDL_dos_audio_synth.h
alongside the existing MPU-401 + OPL3 helper declarations. Engine
(MidiBackendWaveBlaster) doesn't need changes -- it continues calling
SDL_DOSMpu401Init / SDL_DOSMpu401WriteByte / SDL_DOSMpu401Shutdown
unchanged; the path-selection decision lives entirely inside the
SDL helpers.

Dispatch logic in SDL_DOSMpu401Init / WriteByte / Shutdown:
  - default = DSP-mediated (s_mpu401_use_dsp = true, requires
    SDL_DOSAudioSB_IsInitialized() = true; otherwise fail-fast with
    log line so engine can fall back to OPL3 / organya).
  - SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_WB_DIRECT_PORT=1 = direct-port (Option A).
    Body extracted into static SDL_DOSMpu401Init_DirectPort,
    forward-declared at top of synth.c. Body unchanged from patch
    0044 logic: blind init OR opt-in probe via
    SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_PROBE_MPU401=1.

WriteByte additionally drops the previous direct-port poll on bit 6
(DRR) per analysis hard-no #1. Section 9 of the probe demonstrated
direct-port writes succeed BLIND -- no status read needed.

Shutdown is a no-op for the DSP-mediated path (the engine's all-
notes-off MIDI bytes already went through the DSP path before
Shutdown is called; DOSSOUNDBLASTER_CloseDevice's 0xD3 silences
final hold notes). Direct-port path retains the 0xFF reset write
for symmetry with what users opting into that path would expect.

Init-order discipline (the analysis's strongest single recommendation,
hard-no #3): engine must call SDL_DOSMpu401Init AFTER
SDL_AudioBackend_Init has returned AND after the audio thread has
serviced at least one frame. We check IsInitialized() as a minimum
sanity gate; the ">=1 frame serviced" check is intentionally
engine-side because we don't track frame count here. Engine
(nx-engine MidiBackendWaveBlaster) currently calls Init in its
constructor which runs after SoundManager::init() completes -- that
satisfies "audio backend open" but not necessarily ">=1 frame
serviced". If real-HW W22-WB-G iter still hangs at WB init, the
engine-side init order needs further sequencing (nx-engine's lane).

doskutsu_dbg_log lines:
  - DSP-mediated init success: "mpu401: DSP-mediated init at
    port_base=0x%04x (default since patch 0047; DSP cmd 0x34 UART
    entry; set SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_WB_DIRECT_PORT=1 to use
    direct-port path instead)"
  - DSP-mediated init aborted (no SB16): "mpu401: DSP-mediated init
    aborted -- SB16 backend not initialized (engine init order bug)..."
  - Direct-port path: existing 0044 lines preserved.

BOOT.md entry added per env_vars_document_in_user_docs.md:
  SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_WB_DIRECT_PORT=1
  Category: dev-only (LOCKUP RISK on real Vibra16S+S2; default-off
  preserves DSP-mediated safety).

Validation: DOSBox-X smoke is "no regression on organya path" +
"WB-explicit code path runs without crash" only. Real-HW iter on
g2k Vibra16S CT2490 + DreamBlaster S2 is the actual MIDI-audible
gate. Per memory dosbox_not_behavioral_proxy_for_io.md.

Local DOSBox-X smoke matrix passed:
  - organya regression: clean exit 1s, full snd-shutdown trace
  - force-pause regression: clean exit 1s (SDL/0046 + 0043 unaffected)
  - wb-explicit (DSP-mediated default): clean exit 1s, log shows
    "mpu401: DSP-mediated init at port_base=0x0330" + full song-start
    + song-stop + shutdown trace through engine-shutdown[8/8]
  - wb-explicit + WB_DIRECT_PORT=1: clean exit 1s, log shows
    "mpu401: blind init at port_base=0x0330"; legacy 0044 path intact

Modifies:
  vendor/SDL/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c (new exports)
  vendor/SDL/src/core/dos/SDL_dos_audio_synth.h (new declarations)
  vendor/SDL/src/core/dos/SDL_dos_audio_synth.c (path split + dispatch)

docs/BOOT.md edit for the new env var lives in the parent doskutsu
repo (not in this vendor commit).
