+/* ------------------------------------------------------------------------
+ * SB16 DSP-mediated MIDI dispatch helpers (patch 0047)
+ * ------------------------------------------------------------------------
+ *
+ * Used by SDL_DOSMpu401Init/WriteByte when the default DSP-mediated path
+ * is selected (see W22-WB-F MPUPROBE forensic analysis at
+ * docs/MPUPROBE-W22WB-F-ANALYSIS.md). Funnels all chip access through the
+ * DSP write port (base+0xC), eliminating cross-firmware races between
+ * direct-port MPU-401 access and DSP DMA programming that caused the
+ * W22-WB-C/D lockups.
+ *
+ * Implementation lives in src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c next to
+ * WriteSoundBlasterDSP (the underlying DSP I/O primitive). Declared here
+ * so the synth.c MPU-401 wrapper can call them; engine-side WB backend
+ * keeps calling SDL_DOSMpu401Init/WriteByte as before.
+ */
+
+// Returns true if the SB16 audio backend is open (DOSSOUNDBLASTER_OpenDevice
+// completed successfully). Used by SDL_DOSMpu401Init to gate DSP-mediated
+// path on backend availability -- the path requires DSP I/O which only
+// works when the audio backend has detected + initialized the chip. Engine
+// is additionally responsible for ensuring the audio playback thread has
+// serviced at least one frame before WB init (per analysis hard-no #3).
+extern bool SDL_DOSAudioSB_IsInitialized(void);
+
+// Issues DSP cmd 0x34 to enter MPU-401 UART MIDI mode. Subsequent MIDI
+// byte writes go through SDL_DOSAudioSB_DSPMidiWriteByte. No IRQ is
+// generated (probe section 11 confirmed). Caller must IsInitialized()
+// first; calling without DSP open is undefined.
+extern void SDL_DOSAudioSB_DSPMidiEnterUART(void);
+
+// Issues DSP cmd 0x38 + byte payload to dispatch one MIDI byte through
+// the DSP-mediated path. Polls DSP write-status (port 0x22D bit 7) which
+// IS reliable on real hardware (probe section 10 evidence). Two DSP
+// writes per MIDI byte; ~us per write on Pentium.
+extern void SDL_DOSAudioSB_DSPMidiWriteByte(uint8_t byte);
+
 /* ------------------------------------------------------------------------
